WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:02.233
Dependency injection.

2
00:00:02.533 --> 00:00:09.467
This one feature is the difference between tests that need API keys and tests that run offline in seconds.

3
00:00:10.667 --> 00:00:13.433
FastAPI flips construction inside out.

4
00:00:13.733 --> 00:00:20.900
Instead of each route building a database session or an LLM client, it just declares what it needs in its signature.

5
00:00:21.200 --> 00:00:26.567
FastAPI builds it, shares it, and with yield, even cleans it up after the response.

6
00:00:27.767 --> 00:00:30.533
Dependencies can depend on other dependencies.

7
00:00:30.833 --> 00:00:34.033
This route needs an LLM client and the current user.

8
00:00:34.333 --> 00:00:37.704
And the current user itself needs a database session.

9
00:00:37.704 --> 00:00:39.867
FastAPI works out the whole order.

10
00:00:41.067 --> 00:00:42.400
Here's the trick in code.

11
00:00:42.700 --> 00:00:46.533
This function builds the real client, which needs an API key.

12
00:00:46.833 --> 00:00:48.775
The route doesn't build anything.

13
00:00:48.775 --> 00:00:50.833
It just says it depends on get llm.

14
00:00:51.133 --> 00:00:54.700
In a test, we write a tiny fake that returns a canned answer.

15
00:00:55.000 --> 00:00:59.400
Then one line in dependency overrides swaps it in, without touching the route.

16
00:01:00.600 --> 00:01:01.900
Compare the two worlds.

17
00:01:02.200 --> 00:01:05.194
In production, the route gets the real client.

18
00:01:05.194 --> 00:01:06.300
In tests, a fake.

19
00:01:06.600 --> 00:01:08.487
One needs a key and a network.

20
00:01:08.487 --> 00:01:09.933
The other runs offline.

21
00:01:10.233 --> 00:01:11.333
One takes seconds.

22
00:01:11.333 --> 00:01:12.800
The other, milliseconds.

23
00:01:13.100 --> 00:01:16.933
And the route code being tested is exactly what runs in production.

24
00:01:18.133 --> 00:01:19.833
Here's what it buys you in CI.

25
00:01:20.133 --> 00:01:22.133
Your test suite runs on every push.

26
00:01:22.433 --> 00:01:30.267
Both the LLM and the vector database are injected, so CI swaps in a canned LLM and a tiny in-memory retriever.

27
00:01:30.567 --> 00:01:38.267
Forty endpoint tests run offline in three seconds, cost zero tokens, and never flake when an outside service is down.

28
00:01:39.467 --> 00:01:40.150
Let's recap.

29
00:01:40.150 --> 00:01:42.600
Routes declare what they need with Depends.

30
00:01:42.900 --> 00:01:46.233
FastAPI resolves the whole dependency graph.

31
00:01:46.533 --> 00:01:49.367
Dependency overrides swap in fakes for tests.

32
00:01:49.667 --> 00:01:53.054
So tests run offline, on unchanged route code.

33
00:01:53.054 --> 00:01:56.000
Next up: streaming responses with S S E.
